    {
      "id": 71306,
      "name": "arenson9",
      "username": "arenson9",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/arenson9/{size}/1900_2.png",
      "created_at": "2013-08-22T22:37:06.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>The manager at GP Bloomington is Wendy and I'd be happy to offer an introduction, but you probably don't need it. If you're setting up a regular get together, they care much more about whether or not they can trust you to show up and whether or not anyone else will show up than whether or not they are introduced to you by me. Also, despite exchanging email w/ Wendy and talking to her on the phone once, I've never met her in person.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>I've heard there are other game stores in Bloomington, so I recommend you shop around and find the one that works best -- they're happy you are there, they have good hours, they have good snacks, they have a good location, whatever. I think there's a store called something like Common Room Games.</p>",
      "post_number": 4,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:50:25.824Z",
