    {
      "id": 71307,
      "name": "arenson9",
      "username": "arenson9",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/arenson9/{size}/1900_2.png",
      "created_at": "2013-08-22T22:40:04.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Arsenal is unique compared to any other game store I know of in that it's business model is as much or more about selling food then selling games, so they are really keen to have groups in. Now, every game store likes to have players in the store, because there's a chance you'll buy product, but some games are more lucrative than others. People are always buying more kit for Magic The Gathering or Warhammer, so having those games in the shop is great. People want to load up on their arsenal. Sentinels? Not so much. There might be the odd &nbsp;purchase of an expansion or something, but the market gets saturated much more quickly.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Still, the stores are probably happy enough to put you on the schedule as long as you aren't interfering with anything else.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>I think you'll find that the most important thing is to have a core group of people who enjoy playing and enjoy being with each other enough that they want to keep doing it over and over again.</p>",
      "post_number": 5,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:50:25.910Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
